  message: "Fixed in PR #2354 (dev 39bef1108): the signature reads the pattern's left side for a default and writes a destructured parameter whole.\nFILED REPROS RE-RUN on dev 39bef1108 (the item's five one-file variants, closure/t/hizop_1..5):\n1. f({retries = 3} = {}): signature ({retries = 3} = ...), id 4b68f4cca26e3386; f({retries = 3, timeout = 5} = {}): ({retries = 3, timeout = 5} = ...), 08560f5f5f8b5189; f({retries} = {}): ({retries} = ...), eb572034bb65a6e2. Three ids; on dev 05ed6f5fe the first two shared 44f73e7226972199 with signature ({retries = ...).\n2. m({ a, b }, [c, d] = []): ({ a, b }, [c, d] = ...), 6d02fff58c1ef7dc; m({ a, b, e }, [c, d] = []): ({ a, b, e }, [c, d] = ...), fbe62e4dd3b23199. On dev 05ed6f5fe both showed ([c, d] = ...) and shared d3c8d40e7e87e52a.\n(Ids are printed without the scheme label.) MEASURED by the builder: knex 72, hocuspocus 19, nest packages 15 ids moved; the displayed signature changed on 293 nodes over 49 trees.\nNOT CHECKED, filed: a Rust struct-pattern parameter cut at its first colon (read from code, not run): WI-dufoj-bupan-bajab-tumum-nudot-bapus-badak-runap.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/closure/ (out_dev.txt = dev 39bef1108 after the merge, out_base.txt = dev 05ed6f5fe before it; repro trees t/, run.sh, q.py, presplit.py)."  # 8e2f
